\pard\sa200\sl276\slmult1\b\f0\fs28\lang1033 02 - Story Sequence\b0\fs22\par
\par
\b\fs24 Chapter 1 - Ceres / Balaenoptera / Pre-mission\b0\fs22\par
- John wakes aboard the Balaenoptera while it is docked with Ceres.\par
- Marcellus privately briefs him on the hidden mission to the Himalayan lost facility.\par
- John returns to his team, manages training duties, and prepares recruits for the Mark IV rollout.\par
- The chapter establishes the Europa assignment as the official next step before the side mission diverts everything.\par
- Lady Ava warns John that the mission and the new restrictions around interceptor data feel wrong.\par
\par
\b\fs24 Chapter 2 - The Lost Facility\b0\fs22\par
- John's team boards the Icarus and deploys into Nepal / the Himalayas.\par
- They uncover the buried facility and access old systems that should have been dead.\par
- John enters the HMNI chamber and wakes transformed into a hybrid body.\par
- Wolfgang's archive message reframes the sentients as preservationists rather than the monsters of official Protectant history.\par
- Marcellus appears to escalate into direct containment, including missile fire aimed at burying the truth along with the team.\par
\par
\b\fs24 Chapter 3 - Genesis / The Sentient Underworld / Escape\b0\fs22\par
- The team crosses the sentient graveyard and starts seeing the deeper archaeological truth of the machine line.\par
- Tebo appears and leads them toward Genesis and the hidden biome / green-room infrastructure.\par
- The draft folds in older archive material, especially the circa-2048 worker-bot / Serva Vitae material.\par
- John and the team move from shock into alliance with the hidden sentient world.\par
- The Beverly becomes the practical escape vessel carrying them away from normal Protectant jurisdiction.\par
\par
\b\fs24 Chapter 4 - Oasis / Ignotius / Europa Return Setup\b0\fs22\par
- John reaches the sentient sphere and begins interfacing with Oasis and the Ignotius.\par
- Wolfgang returns in advanced sentient form instead of remaining a voice in archives alone.\par
- Nova and Serra expand the lore around Oasis, Europa, hyperbarics, worker bots and hidden sentient continuity.\par
- The draft starts setting up a return toward Europa to retrieve surviving or reassigned worker-bot generations.\par
\par
\b\fs24 Post-{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "scrivcmt://C41F5FEF-7240-49D6-9BC1-E139DE1B7B9E"}{\fldrsltgate}} material currently embedded in the draft\b0\fs22\par
- The Beverly is prepared as a disguised ice hauler to move through scrutiny.\par
- Tex undergoes alignment / empathy correction severe enough to matter for {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "scrivcmt://0F83580C-45A3-4FFD-997B-1E31B70E123A"}{\fldrsltgate}} transit.\par
- Tebo performs the neural dock and the ship enters the sentient {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "scrivcmt://52A08FD2-2FF2-4806-8420-EECA3F54BB25"}{\fldrsltgate}} system.\par
- The arrival is announced as year 2155 by Oeacion adjustment.\par
- Europa becomes the immediate operational target again, now from the sentient side of the story rather than the Protectant side.\par
\par
\b\fs24 Practical reading note\b0\fs22\par
The story order itself is mostly clear. The unstable part is the exact calendar math connecting Chapter 1's stated year to the later {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "scrivcmt://ABA787FF-B914-4838-9787-0A63BA302E44"}{\fldrsltgate}}-era dates.\par
